{
  "name": "Get new job postings from 17,000+ company career sites into Google Sheets every day",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Get new job postings from 17,000+ company career sites into Google Sheets every day\n\nEvery morning this workflow pulls only the jobs posted since the last run that match your job titles and locations, straight from employers' own career sites (Greenhouse, Lever, Ashby, Workday, SmartRecruiters, Workable and more), and appends them to a Google Sheet. No LinkedIn or Indeed scraping, no reposts, no logins.\n\n**Who it's for:** job seekers running a targeted search, recruiters tracking a role family, niche job boards.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Schedule Trigger** runs every day at 8:00.\n2. **Set your job search** holds the titles, locations and limits you edit.\n3. **HTTP Request** calls the Apify *Job Postings API* Actor (`cleanrowdata/fresh-jobs-index`) with `onlyNewSinceLastRun`, so each run returns (and bills) only jobs you have not seen.\n4. **Keep sheet columns** keeps 7 fields and **Google Sheets** appends one row per job. If there are no new jobs, nothing is written.\n\n### Setup\n1. Create a free [Apify](https://apify.com) account and copy your API token (Settings > API & Integrations).\n2. In the HTTP Request node create a **Header Auth** credential: Name `Authorization`, Value `Bearer YOUR_APIFY_TOKEN`.\n3. Edit **Set your job search** (comma-separated lists). Adding `Remote` to locations also matches remote jobs in other countries.\n4. Create a Google Sheet with headers `posted_at, company, title, location, salary_text, ats, job_url`, connect Google Sheets and select the sheet.\n\n### Requirements\nApify account (pay per job: $2.50 per 1,000 on the free plan, which includes $5/month of credit), Google Sheets.\n\n### Customization\nAdd filters to the JSON body (`minSalaryUsd`, `seniority`, `remoteOnly`, `companies`), or swap Google Sheets for Slack, Notion, Airtable or email.",
        "height": 820,
        "width": 560,
        "color": 1
      },
      "id": "c4a74c5b-216d-57f8-a54c-b727b6994987",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -640,
        -260
      ]
